  "term": "task demands",
  "definition": "Task demands are the specific requirements of an activity that shape how a person controls perception and action while doing it. In this source, they refer to differences such as only tracking a moving target versus tracking it while also intercepting it, which changed how visual feedback and prediction were used during eye movement control.",
